## Purpose

The current branch has reached a coherent and working checkpoint:

- a Journey contains ordered Steps;
- JourneyProgress advances through them;
- Tell and Ask Steps are persisted and loaded through Drift;
- Journey remains ignorant of concrete Step behaviour;
- Tell and Ask presentation components are self-contained;
- onboarding Tell copy, timing, and Setup Assistant-inspired presentation have been exercised in the real debug application;
- 30-SYSTEM-BOUNDARIES.md records current proven boundaries.

The next work is explicitly speculative.

We want to test whether:

- a Step may be implemented by a child Journey;
- Journeys can remain linear;
- only upward signals are required;
- early successful completion can replace arbitrary branching;
- the model can explain the Full Disk Access workflow without creating spaghetti.

The current working implementation must therefore be preserved before that experiment begins.

